{
  "comment": [
    "GraalVM native-image cannot see java.lang.foreign calls the way it sees ordinary",
    "code: a FunctionDescriptor is a runtime value, so the build needs to be told which",
    "native signatures the executable is allowed to call. Without this file the program",
    "still compiles and then dies on the first downcall with MissingForeignRegistrationError.",
    "",
    "Generated by running the app under -agentlib:native-image-agent, which records the",
    "signatures actually exercised, then reviewed by hand. The three entries marked with a",
    "reason below are NOT in the generated set: they belong to ObjC helper methods the",
    "current Main never calls (sendRect, sendVoidRect, sendLong), and leaving them out",
    "would make this file a landmine for the next caller rather than a description of what",
    "the code may do.",
    "",
    "Signature vocabulary: 'void*' is a pointer, 'jlong'/'jint'/'jbyte' are the scalar",
    "carriers, and 'struct(...)' is a by-value aggregate -- here NSRect, which is what makes",
    "Objective-C's initWithContentRect:styleMask:backing:defer: work at all.",
    "",
    "Note: the schema shipped inside GraalVM advertises a per-entry 'reason' field, but the",
    "parser rejects it ('Unknown attribute(s) [reason] in foreign call'), so the explanations",
    "of the hand-added entries live here instead. Order of the list below: msgSend signatures",
    "first, then the two by-value NSRect call shapes, then the three unused helper signatures,",
    "then the libobjc / dlopen / pthread entry points.",
    "The UI-thread hop (io.github.lihuu.panamaview.macos.UiThread) adds one more downcall shape -- void(void*,void*,void*) for dispatch_async_f, already listed above -- and one direct upcall, drain. _dispatch_main_q is a data symbol, so it needs no downcall entry.",
    "handleDidStartNavigation is the page-unload hook: it lets the bridge abandon every in-flight request when the document that made them goes away.",
    "resources lists only the framework's own asset, the client bridge. It must NOT list anything else: a consumer's native build applies this file transitively, so any page named here would be embedded into every consumer's binary. The demo app in demo-app/ passes -H:IncludeResources='web/.*' on its own command line instead, which is exactly how a consumer embeds its own assets.",
    "AssetSchemeHandler serves the app's assets over a private URL scheme instead of file://, because an opaque file:// origin refuses ES modules, fetch and Workers. It adds one downcall shape -- NSHTTPURLResponse's initWithURL:statusCode:HTTPVersion:headerFields: takes four objects and an NSInteger -- and two upcalls for the WKURLSchemeHandler protocol.",
    "dataWithBytes:length: needs an object followed by an NSInteger -- the reverse of representationUsingType:properties:, so it is a separate registered shape.",
    "Notifications adds UNUserNotificationCenter: two block callbacks (handleAuthorization, handlePost) and one downcall shape -- requestAuthorizationWithOptions:completionHandler: takes an NSUInteger followed by a block."
  ],
